{
 "id": "past-simple",
 "title": "Le prétérit (past simple)",
 "level": "A2",
 "topic": "Temps verbaux",
 "summary": "Raconter ce qui est fini : verbes réguliers, irréguliers à connaître, did pour la négation et la question.",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "Quand l'utiliser ?"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Pour une action **terminée** à un moment **précis du passé**, mentionné ou sous-entendu : *yesterday, last week, in 2019, two days ago.*"
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "Verbes réguliers : + ed"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "head": [
    "Règle",
    "Exemple"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "la plupart : + ed",
     "work → worked"
    ],
    [
     "-e : + d",
     "live → lived"
    ],
    [
     "consonne + y → ied",
     "study → studied"
    ],
    [
     "CVC : on double",
     "stop → stopped"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "La prononciation de **-ed** : /t/ après un son sourd (*worked*), /d/ après un son voisé (*played*), /ɪd/ après t ou d (*wanted*)."
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "Verbes irréguliers fréquents"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "head": [
    "Base",
    "Passé",
    "Base",
    "Passé"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "be",
     "was / were",
     "go",
     "went"
    ],
    [
     "have",
     "had",
     "see",
     "saw"
    ],
    [
     "do",
     "did",
     "take",
     "took"
    ],
    [
     "make",
     "made",
     "buy",
     "bought"
    ],
    [
     "get",
     "got",
     "write",
     "wrote"
    ],
    [
     "know",
     "knew",
     "think",
     "thought"
    ],
    [
     "come",
     "came",
     "send",
     "sent"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "Négation et question"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "On utilise **did** (pour toutes les personnes). Le verbe repasse à l'infinitif : *I **didn't go***, ***Did** you **go**?*"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Avec **to be**, pas de did : *I wasn't there. Were you there?*"
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "Exemples"
  },
  {
   "type": "ex",
   "en": "I sent the file yesterday.",
   "fr": "J'ai envoyé le fichier hier."
  },
  {
   "type": "ex",
   "en": "She didn't come to the meeting.",
   "fr": "Elle n'est pas venue à la réunion."
  },
  {
   "type": "ex",
   "en": "Did you see the update?",
   "fr": "As-tu vu la mise à jour ?"
  },
  {
   "type": "ex",
   "en": "We moved to Lyon in 2018.",
   "fr": "Nous avons déménagé à Lyon en 2018."
  },
  {
   "type": "tip",
   "text": "**Piège** : « Je suis allé » se traduit par *I went* (past simple) quand le moment est précis. L'anglais n'a pas de passé composé équivalent pour ça."
  }
 ],
